-- A GIVEN of its own does not excuse a line written like a mixfix rule when
-- the GIVEN names no input where the rule has its word: `Red` is not an input
-- of this GIVEN, and `costs` is not either, so the line is still refused, once.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
c `costs` n MEANS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
Red `costs` n MEANS 1

#EVAL Red `costs` 0
